- For one hour, modernising!

780
00:27:37,777 --> 00:27:40,260
- To the foreign Annikki.

781
00:27:40,260 --> 00:27:43,802
If you find her alone,
bring her quickly back!

782
00:27:43,802 --> 00:27:47,420
So that she may become my prisoner!

783
00:27:47,420 --> 00:27:50,301
- Well she's one sheet to the wind.

784
00:27:50,301 --> 00:27:53,436
- Wait a minute, I forgot something, oh!

785
00:27:53,436 --> 00:27:56,565
- Grandma's been talking
to the bedding again.

786
00:27:56,565 --> 00:27:59,943
- You really get a lot of
use out of a good wool cape.

787
00:27:59,943 --> 00:28:01,422
- We'll be cruising today at an altitude

788
00:28:01,422 --> 00:28:03,339
of about 60 feet or so.

789
00:28:05,982 --> 00:28:07,604
- Well, let's see now, what did she say?

790
00:28:07,604 --> 00:28:09,919
Go to something, and get something, uh,

791
00:28:09,919 --> 00:28:10,836
from, yeah.

792
00:28:11,719 --> 00:28:13,262
- Please remain seated until the cape

793
00:28:13,262 --> 00:28:15,538
has come to a complete stop, thank you.

794
00:28:15,538 --> 00:28:16,718
- Hmm?

795
00:28:16,718 --> 00:28:18,750
Oh, don't tell me
Hercules is in this movie!

796
00:28:18,750 --> 00:28:20,215
- Hercules is in this movie.

797
00:28:20,215 --> 00:28:21,597
- Oh, I asked you not to tell me that!

798
00:28:21,597 --> 00:28:23,431
- Oh, the cabin boy, the cabin boy,

799
00:28:23,431 --> 00:28:25,502
the dirty little birdie!

800
00:28:25,502 --> 00:28:27,419
(hums)

801
00:28:31,746 --> 00:28:33,996
- Hey, uh, how'd I do that?

802
00:28:35,537 --> 00:28:38,746
- Boy, kidnapping was
really easy back then!

803
00:28:38,746 --> 00:28:39,829
- Oh, Popeye!

804
00:28:41,060 --> 00:28:42,848
- He's large.

805
00:28:42,848 --> 00:28:44,270
- Dun, dun, dun, huh?

806
00:28:44,270 --> 00:28:45,103
The hell?

807
00:28:46,483 --> 00:28:47,908
- There's a roast in the oven!

808
00:28:47,908 --> 00:28:50,491
I don't know when I'll be back!

809
00:28:52,913 --> 00:28:53,746
- Oh boy.

810
00:28:55,718 --> 00:28:57,301
- The secret storm!

811
00:28:59,621 --> 00:29:01,735
- Da weather started gettin' rough,

812
00:29:01,735 --> 00:29:04,735
- [Robots] the tiny ship was tossed!

813
00:29:05,754 --> 00:29:07,056
- There's a flash flood warning

814
00:29:07,056 --> 00:29:09,389
affecting Stonehenge region!

815
00:29:13,064 --> 00:29:14,870
- By the pricking of my thumb,

816
00:29:14,870 --> 00:29:17,453
something goofy this way comes.

817
00:29:21,528 --> 00:29:22,945
- Come on, doggy.

818
00:29:27,203 --> 00:29:29,592
- Geez, thanks for the lift!

819
00:29:29,592 --> 00:29:33,175
- Call the front desk
if you need anything!

820
00:29:36,464 --> 00:29:37,464
- I got one!

821
00:29:40,495 --> 00:29:43,096
- Hey, get me, I'm Swedish
and I've got rhythm!

822
00:29:43,096 --> 00:29:45,179
- I sing whenever I sing!

823
00:29:46,514 --> 00:29:47,609
- Ilmarinen!

824
00:29:47,609 --> 00:29:49,479
- It's three in the morning!

825
00:29:49,479 --> 00:29:51,961
- The evil witch Louhi
has stolen your sister!

826
00:29:51,961 --> 00:29:53,262
- Yeah, and?

827
00:29:53,262 --> 00:29:54,095
- Annikki!

828
00:29:55,525 --> 00:29:57,547
- Here, wait a minute,
let me put my sword out.

829
00:29:57,547 --> 00:29:58,380
There.

830
00:29:59,738 --> 00:30:01,687
- Give me the sword!

831
00:30:01,687 --> 00:30:03,437
I will go to Pohjola!

832
00:30:05,465 --> 00:30:08,105
- Ah, let me just finish up here.

833
00:30:08,105 --> 00:30:08,938
So there!

834
00:30:10,710 --> 00:30:12,580
Say hi to my sister!

835
00:30:12,580 --> 00:30:15,381
- I will go with you to
Pohjola, Lemminkainen!

836
00:30:15,381 --> 00:30:16,847
- Wait, I'll drive.

837
00:30:16,847 --> 00:30:17,987
Let me get my keys.

838
00:30:17,987 --> 00:30:18,820
There we go.

839
00:30:18,820 --> 00:30:20,737
(hums)

840
00:30:22,621 --> 00:30:24,127
- Vainamoinen!

841
00:30:24,127 --> 00:30:25,428
My sister has been stolen!

842
00:30:25,428 --> 00:30:26,648
- Well, was she insured?

843
00:30:26,648 --> 00:30:28,598
- By the evil witch, Louhi!

844
00:30:28,598 --> 00:30:30,225
- Looks kind of like a Bible story.

845
00:30:30,225 --> 00:30:31,367
- Tell us, Vainamoinen!

846
00:30:31,367 --> 00:30:32,705
Tell us how we can find our way

847
00:30:32,705 --> 00:30:34,494
to the misty shores of Pohjola!

848
00:30:34,494 --> 00:30:36,240
- Go down to the third stoplight, and...

849
00:30:36,240 --> 00:30:38,315
- Ah, Pohjola, the edge of the world.

850
00:30:38,315 --> 00:30:40,388
If you want to go there,

851
00:30:40,388 --> 00:30:42,991
- Take the Santa Monica freeway.

852
00:30:42,991 --> 00:30:45,920
- It will carry you over
the waves like a white swan.

853
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:47,791
- Tell us, mighty one.

854
00:30:47,791 --> 00:30:50,440
How can we build a boat such as that?

855
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:51,417
- I'm glad you asked.

856
00:30:51,417 --> 00:30:53,852
I'm having a boat-building seminar.

857
00:30:53,852 --> 00:30:57,025
- In this ancient oak tree
you will find your boat.

858
00:30:57,025 --> 00:30:59,625
Whereupon you take it
out, and it will carry you

859
00:30:59,625 --> 00:31:02,801
across the sea to the shores of Pohjola.

860
00:31:02,801 --> 00:31:06,384
- Okay, how much is
this gonna set me back?

861
00:31:09,307 --> 00:31:11,583
- Oh, I'm a-chafin like me!

862
00:31:11,583 --> 00:31:13,166
Oops, did it again.

863
00:31:14,426 --> 00:31:17,382
- You're kidding me, a boat in here?

864
00:31:17,382 --> 00:31:19,925
- It's a chip-away game.

865
00:31:19,925 --> 00:31:22,971
- Is there another wise
man we could talk to?

866
00:31:22,971 --> 00:31:25,090
- Eight years later...

867
00:31:25,090 --> 00:31:27,524
- So anyway, that's what
really got me interested

868
00:31:27,524 --> 00:31:28,864
in stamp collecting.

869
00:31:28,864 --> 00:31:30,369
Of course, I've always loved the theater.

870
00:31:30,369 --> 00:31:31,619
- Just shut up.

871
00:31:34,225 --> 00:31:36,622
(tree creaking)

872
00:31:36,622 --> 00:31:37,872
- Hey, no boat!

873
00:31:38,985 --> 00:31:42,235
- That's my scratching tree, you jerks!

874
00:31:44,391 --> 00:31:45,724
- Not that tree.

875
00:31:49,724 --> 00:31:50,982
(stifling laughter)

876
00:31:50,982 --> 00:31:55,638
- Ah, Fred, did I mention
that I have a boat?

877
00:31:55,638 --> 00:31:58,553
Oh, now they're just showing off.

878
00:31:58,553 --> 00:32:01,034
- Oh, now what did they
chop the sail out of?

879
00:32:01,034 --> 00:32:02,417
- Oh, they cut the wood real thin.

880
00:32:02,417 --> 00:32:03,250
- Uh-huh.

881
00:32:04,248 --> 00:32:08,069
- May the sun light the way to
bring you safely home again.

882
00:32:08,069 --> 00:32:10,061
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, can
the balloon juice, Gramps,

883
00:32:10,061 --> 00:32:10,894
we're out of here.

884
00:32:10,894 --> 00:32:14,901
- Hey, shouldn't we
patch the bottom first?

885
00:32:14,901 --> 00:32:18,151
- I just pray there aren't no portages.

886
00:32:19,287 --> 00:32:20,120
- Oh boy.

887
00:32:20,120 --> 00:32:23,456
The Stay Puft Marshmallow Man in chains?

888
00:32:23,456 --> 00:32:24,289
- Kinky.

889
00:32:25,408 --> 00:32:27,441
It's giant sweet breads.

890
00:32:27,441 --> 00:32:28,858
- It's body wars.

891
00:32:30,570 --> 00:32:33,418
- Someone has come to visit us!

892
00:32:33,418 --> 00:32:34,761
- Quick, pick up the place!

893
00:32:34,761 --> 00:32:37,220
Make yourself presentable!

894
00:32:37,220 --> 00:32:38,853
- [Male voice] Over here!

895
00:32:38,853 --> 00:32:40,316
It's me!

896
00:32:40,316 --> 00:32:43,250
- What, it's a bag of Homer Simpson?

897
00:32:43,250 --> 00:32:44,444
(all crying out)

898
00:32:44,444 --> 00:32:47,206
- Wait, one at a time, please, come on.

899
00:32:47,206 --> 00:32:48,143
- [Woman] Yes!

900
00:32:48,143 --> 00:32:50,093
I am the South Wind!

901
00:32:50,093 --> 00:32:53,450
- Do you provide a service of some sort?

902
00:32:53,450 --> 00:32:56,857
- [Male Voice 2] And
I, I am the East Wind!

903
00:32:56,857 --> 00:33:01,211
- Put your teeth in, I
can't understand you!

904
00:33:01,211 --> 00:33:03,815
- Are you the North Wind?

905
00:33:03,815 --> 00:33:05,969
- I am the Mists.

906
00:33:05,969 --> 00:33:07,793
- I'm relative humidity.

907
00:33:07,793 --> 00:33:10,113
It's not so much the heat as it is me.

908
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:13,696
- I'm the summer wind
that come blowin' in.

909
00:33:16,802 --> 00:33:17,635
- And you!

910
00:33:17,635 --> 00:33:18,468
(giggling)

911
00:33:18,468 --> 00:33:19,374
Which one are you?

912
00:33:19,374 --> 00:33:20,922
- Oh me? I'm just the laundry.

913
00:33:20,922 --> 00:33:22,998
- I am the North Wind.

914
00:33:22,998 --> 00:33:24,096
- Call me Sandy.

915
00:33:24,096 --> 00:33:26,346
- I was born among the ice.

916
00:33:27,226 --> 00:33:30,759
- Oh, that's fine, thank you, heh heh.

917
00:33:30,759 --> 00:33:32,876
- Please let me out!

918
00:33:32,876 --> 00:33:34,912
- Yeah, I didn't ask for a biography.

919
00:33:34,912 --> 00:33:38,247
- Very well, I will let you out.

920
00:33:38,247 --> 00:33:41,713
- [Louhi] So, this is where I find you!

921
00:33:41,713 --> 00:33:43,744
- Oh, we weren't kissing,
we were just talking!

922
00:33:43,744 --> 00:33:46,303
- It's something to amuse you.

923
00:33:46,303 --> 00:33:50,165
Just come with me, I'll
find something for you.

924
00:33:50,165 --> 00:33:52,442
- I've got one of those little pool tables

925
00:33:52,442 --> 00:33:54,106
I bought at Brookstone.

926
00:33:54,106 --> 00:33:56,265
- Hold my prisoner in chains!

927
00:33:56,265 --> 00:33:59,132
- Alright, some orders we like to get!

928
00:33:59,132 --> 00:34:00,132
- Let me go!

929
00:34:01,197 --> 00:34:03,780
(techno music)

930
00:34:06,709 --> 00:34:08,042
- Deep thoughts.

931
00:34:09,966 --> 00:34:11,147
- Oh, Walleye Chop!

932
00:34:11,147 --> 00:34:13,951
I'd better get out there!

933
00:34:13,951 --> 00:34:15,773
- Eric's small cigars.

934
00:34:15,773 --> 00:34:17,198
- Inconceivable!

935
00:34:17,198 --> 00:34:18,702
They're gaining on us!

936
00:34:18,702 --> 00:34:20,085
Oh, the keg's here!

937
00:34:20,085 --> 00:34:22,723
- Aye, he has come, as I said he would.

938
00:34:22,723 --> 00:34:24,752
Do you see his boat approaching our shore?

939
00:34:24,752 --> 00:34:26,863
Do you hear the waves bringing him nearer?

940
00:34:26,863 --> 00:34:27,920
Come, wake up!

941
00:34:27,920 --> 00:34:29,711
Run to the beach and welcome him!

942
00:34:29,711 --> 00:34:32,920
- You're the boss, you're
the queen of everything, ok.

943
00:34:32,920 --> 00:34:35,170
- Smiles, everyone, smiles!

944
00:34:38,107 --> 00:34:40,248
- Hey, do you have a dock or something?

945
00:34:40,248 --> 00:34:42,893
We'd really appreciate it.

946
00:34:42,893 --> 00:34:44,237
- Huh, look at that boat.

947
00:34:44,237 --> 00:34:45,822
What, did you carve it out of a tree?

948
00:34:45,822 --> 00:34:47,405
- Shut up, shut up!

949
00:34:48,843 --> 00:34:50,670
- [Wizard] Mistress!

950
00:34:50,670 --> 00:34:52,090
Oh, you were right!

951
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:53,758
The boat is bringing Lemminkainen,

952
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:56,038
and his friend, the immortal blacksmith,

953
00:34:56,038 --> 00:34:56,871
Ilmarinen!

954
00:34:58,590 --> 00:35:00,479
- Greetings for all!

955
00:35:00,479 --> 00:35:02,601
Who accepts the challenge
that I have brought?

956
00:35:02,601 --> 00:35:03,863
- Can't, got a bad knee.

957
00:35:03,863 --> 00:35:04,958
- I did the last challenge.

958
00:35:04,958 --> 00:35:07,190
- I have come to free the maid Annikki!

959
00:35:07,190 --> 00:35:08,494
I am here with her brother.

960
00:35:08,494 --> 00:35:09,671
- Uh, Tony.

961
00:35:09,671 --> 00:35:10,648
- You are no coward.

962
00:35:10,648 --> 00:35:11,481
- No coward?

963
00:35:11,481 --> 00:35:12,519
- Then fight!

964
00:35:12,519 --> 00:35:15,726
If your power can protect
you from my arrows.

965
00:35:15,726 --> 00:35:17,557
- Yes, my power is great.

966
00:35:17,557 --> 00:35:19,387
- Ah, it's not that fun
- [Louhi] Magics!

967
00:35:19,387 --> 00:35:20,607
going to Grandma's anymore.

968
00:35:20,607 --> 00:35:22,235
- And charms.

969
00:35:22,235 --> 00:35:24,432
And terrible spells
enough to drive you back

970
00:35:24,432 --> 00:35:26,344
into the boiling cove
from which you've come,

971
00:35:26,344 --> 00:35:27,886
you blundering fool!

972
00:35:27,886 --> 00:35:29,471
- That's enough of that.

973
00:35:29,471 --> 00:35:30,524
Do you imagine we've come here

974
00:35:30,524 --> 00:35:32,068
to listen to an old woman raving?

975
00:35:32,068 --> 00:35:33,290
- That's why most people come!

976
00:35:33,290 --> 00:35:34,714
- Now, do you accept the challenge,

977
00:35:34,714 --> 00:35:36,547
or will you give up my sister without it?

978
00:35:36,547 --> 00:35:37,848
- Take the curtain, go for the box!

979
00:35:37,848 --> 00:35:40,211
- I will not give up Annikki.

980
00:35:40,211 --> 00:35:41,999
- Here she busts, the witch is brittle!

981
00:35:41,999 --> 00:35:42,936
- No, wait!

982
00:35:42,936 --> 00:35:44,195
- Let me take off my girdle!

983
00:35:44,195 --> 00:35:46,267
- I will give your maiden back to you,

984
00:35:46,267 --> 00:35:48,623
if you perform two simple tasks.

985
00:35:48,623 --> 00:35:50,695
- Aw, this bites, let's blow.

986
00:35:50,695 --> 00:35:51,528
- What tasks?

987
00:35:51,528 --> 00:35:53,709
- Pick up my dry cleaning
and call the vet.

988
00:35:53,709 --> 00:35:56,101
- I have a field overrun with snakes,

989
00:35:56,101 --> 00:35:58,346
and he must first plow it!

990
00:35:58,346 --> 00:35:59,179
- Alright.

991
00:35:59,179 --> 00:36:01,612
- It's weird, but...

992
00:36:01,612 --> 00:36:02,957
- Show me where your field is.

993
00:36:02,957 --> 00:36:06,124
- Come on, come on, good Lemminkaimen.

994
00:36:08,627 --> 00:36:10,540
- Don't wait up, Eric,
if you know what I mean.

995
00:36:10,540 --> 00:36:12,207
- Say, that is cold.

996
00:36:15,911 --> 00:36:17,946
- You see it before you.

997
00:36:17,946 --> 00:36:20,348
- You see an old grackle.

998
00:36:20,348 --> 00:36:22,664
- A field of snakes.

999
00:36:22,664 --> 00:36:24,374
- Hey, Kevin Costner's in that, isn't he?

1000
00:36:24,374 --> 00:36:25,555
- No, this is the dirty version.

1001
00:36:25,555 --> 00:36:26,388
- Oh.

1002
00:36:27,512 --> 00:36:28,975
- I want a plow.

1003
00:36:28,975 --> 00:36:31,454
And I must have a powerful horse with it.

1004
00:36:31,454 --> 00:36:33,003
- Nay, I'm the cursed boss here.

1005
00:36:33,003 --> 00:36:34,182
- Are you asking me to feed

1006
00:36:34,182 --> 00:36:36,590
one of my horses to those snakes?

1007
00:36:36,590 --> 00:36:37,892
- He needs a horse.

1008
00:36:37,892 --> 00:36:39,237
I will build him a horse.

1009
00:36:39,237 --> 00:36:41,570
- Oh, make it out of a tree!

1010
00:36:43,102 --> 00:36:44,745
- Horse chestnut.

1011
00:36:44,745 --> 00:36:45,923
- [Wizard] Oh, Mistress!

1012
00:36:45,923 --> 00:36:47,184
- Don't call me that in public!

1013
00:36:47,184 --> 00:36:48,184
- Come here!

1014
00:36:49,633 --> 00:36:53,013
You must not allow Ilmarinen
to build that horse!

1015
00:36:53,013 --> 00:36:54,883
He'll be sure to plow the field,

1016
00:36:54,883 --> 00:36:56,669
and they will take Annikki!

1017
00:36:56,669 --> 00:36:59,150
Ilmarinen will refuse to make us a Sampo!

1018
00:36:59,150 --> 00:37:00,286
- Have patience!

1019
00:37:00,286 --> 00:37:02,897
He won't be able to carry her away.

1020
00:37:02,897 --> 00:37:04,861
- Now, slip into that stable boy suit

1021
00:37:04,861 --> 00:37:06,449
and meet me later down by the...

1022
00:37:06,449 --> 00:37:08,601
(whispering, laughing)

1023
00:37:08,601 --> 00:37:10,721
- Mistress of mine.

1024
00:37:10,721 --> 00:37:13,288
(men yelling)

1025
00:37:13,288 --> 00:37:14,121
- Oh, wow.

1026
00:37:15,076 --> 00:37:17,395
- And the sculling crew takes to the lake!

1027
00:37:17,395 --> 00:37:19,471
- We've got to get organized!

1028
00:37:19,471 --> 00:37:22,054
- [All] Attica! Attica! Attica!

1029
00:37:22,968 --> 00:37:25,247
- It's the Oslo riots!

1030
00:37:25,247 --> 00:37:28,051
- Hey uh, that's not very
smart when you're in the boat.

1031
00:37:28,051 --> 00:37:29,840
- He is pounding the air there.

1032
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:30,673
- That's an air hammer.

1033
00:37:30,673 --> 00:37:31,506
- Ooh!

1034
00:37:33,215 --> 00:37:35,538
- Hey, we're going over
to Sven's after, huh?

1035
00:37:35,538 --> 00:37:36,371
Want to?

1036
00:37:37,525 --> 00:37:38,462
- Hmm?

1037
00:37:38,462 --> 00:37:40,247
- Suddenly it's flash dance!

1038
00:37:40,247 --> 00:37:43,013
- He's a steel town Sven
on a Saturday night!

1039
00:37:43,013 --> 00:37:45,846
(hammer thudding)

1040
00:37:46,912 --> 00:37:49,316
- Okay, okay, if he can make a horse,

1041
00:37:49,316 --> 00:37:52,934
why'd he have to cut that tree down?

1042
00:37:52,934 --> 00:37:54,396
- Yeah, well, now I just sit back

1043
00:37:54,396 --> 00:37:56,883
and rake in the praise, pretty much.

1044
00:37:56,883 --> 00:37:59,034
- Ooh, Daddy, ooh!

1045
00:37:59,034 --> 00:38:00,819
- The Tri-star logo's ready!

1046
00:38:00,819 --> 00:38:02,445
- He's...

1047
00:38:02,445 --> 00:38:03,278
Safe!

1048
00:38:07,974 --> 00:38:10,391
- They ran calling wild-fire!

1049
00:38:11,473 --> 00:38:12,306
- Ooh!

1050
00:38:13,751 --> 00:38:15,661
Ouch, ooh, stingy, that's still hot!

1051
00:38:15,661 --> 00:38:17,369
- Tsst, haha, tsst!

1052
00:38:17,369 --> 00:38:19,439
- Hello, I'm from the temp agency,

1053
00:38:19,439 --> 00:38:21,689
I'm your horse for the day!

1054
00:38:23,466 --> 00:38:26,110
- Ooh, must be the plow.

1055
00:38:26,110 --> 00:38:27,251
- Hey, good timing!

1056
00:38:27,251 --> 00:38:29,811
Boy, we work good together!

1057
00:38:29,811 --> 00:38:34,082
- Could you rub some
Solarcane on me, please?

1058
00:38:34,082 --> 00:38:35,261
- A horse?

1059
00:38:35,261 --> 00:38:37,377
We didn't plan on that!

1060
00:38:37,377 --> 00:38:40,750
- Will someone please turn the Wagner off?

1061
00:38:40,750 --> 00:38:43,349
- Hey, I think he just
invented the Mobile logo.

1062
00:38:43,349 --> 00:38:44,182
- Hmm!

1063
00:38:51,283 --> 00:38:52,116
- Yech!

1064
00:38:54,799 --> 00:38:57,404
Kind of a goofy Scandinavian double-dare.

1065
00:38:57,404 --> 00:38:59,904
(men yelling)

1066
00:39:00,779 --> 00:39:02,366
- Oh, man, it's a puppet, look.

1067
00:39:02,366 --> 00:39:04,686
- He's being attacked by a woozle.

1068
00:39:04,686 --> 00:39:07,970
- Yeah, they're, they're
all yelling, "Fake!"

1069
00:39:07,970 --> 00:39:10,843
- And now, I'd like to do my
Nostowsya Kimski impression.

1070
00:39:10,843 --> 00:39:13,777
I'll just take off my clothes.

1071
00:39:13,777 --> 00:39:17,527
- I knew they'd worm
their way into the film.

1072
00:39:19,025 --> 00:39:20,052
- You know, I wonder if that horse

1073
00:39:20,052 --> 00:39:22,219
comes in any other colors.

1074
00:39:24,009 --> 00:39:24,904
- Well, he's the enemy,

1075
00:39:24,904 --> 00:39:26,003
but you gotta admire him.

1076
00:39:26,003 --> 00:39:27,791
- Yup, yup, tip your cap.

1077
00:39:27,791 --> 00:39:29,226
- Hey.

1078
00:39:29,226 --> 00:39:31,226
Get a look at this, huh?

1079
00:39:32,151 --> 00:39:36,952
- Now let's go in and see
if Mom's got dinner ready.

1080
00:39:36,952 --> 00:39:40,452
- Oh, great, we can plant more snakes now.

1081
00:39:41,719 --> 00:39:44,519
- Alright, I've finished
plowing your field.

1082
00:39:44,519 --> 00:39:45,903
- Planted now with care.

1083
00:39:45,903 --> 00:39:49,360
And may the grain grow
as high as my shoulder.

1084
00:39:49,360 --> 00:39:50,544
- Now where is she?

1085
00:39:50,544 --> 00:39:52,864
We want to take her back!

1086
00:39:52,864 --> 00:39:54,976
- I'll give you your Annikki,

1087
00:39:54,976 --> 00:39:57,412
but it won't do you much good.

1088
00:39:57,412 --> 00:39:59,778
There isn't very much left of your boat.

1089
00:39:59,778 --> 00:40:01,567
- Hey, that's below the belt.

1090
00:40:01,567 --> 00:40:04,327
- Yeah, I don't really get witches' humor.

1091
00:40:04,327 --> 00:40:07,461
- Come along, let me show you!

1092
00:40:07,461 --> 00:40:10,211
- Brother, she's got issues, huh?

1093
00:40:12,908 --> 00:40:14,899
- It's the Swedish dells!

1094
00:40:14,899 --> 00:40:16,982
The Dukes ride the Dukes.

1095
00:40:18,559 --> 00:40:23,099
- Hey, you wrecked our boat,
you freaked-out maniac!

1096
00:40:23,099 --> 00:40:26,055
- [Louhi] A great fish
swimming near the shore.

1097
00:40:26,055 --> 00:40:30,248
It flipped its tail once,
and smashed your boat!

1098
00:40:30,248 --> 00:40:32,242
- Well I suppose those
kind of things hap--what?

1099
00:40:32,242 --> 00:40:33,785
- Then I will make a new boat!

1100
00:40:33,785 --> 00:40:34,803
An iron one!

1101
00:40:34,803 --> 00:40:36,836
And tell your fish if he
tries to smash this one,

1102
00:40:36,836 --> 00:40:38,298
it'll break his teeth off!

1103
00:40:38,298 --> 00:40:40,620
- Well, you don't have to yell.

1104
00:40:40,620 --> 00:40:41,453
- Huh?

1105
00:40:42,613 --> 00:40:46,296
(Ilmarinen chanting)
- They're roasting Bullwinkle!

1106
00:40:46,296 --> 00:40:47,379
- Come forth!

1107
00:40:50,842 --> 00:40:52,917
- Feed me, Rocky, help me!

1108
00:40:52,917 --> 00:40:53,750
- Again?

1109
00:40:54,709 --> 00:40:56,781
- Oh, nobody ever helps this guy.

1110
00:40:56,781 --> 00:40:57,842
- Look! A boat!

1111
00:40:57,842 --> 00:40:59,668
(all crying out)

1112
00:40:59,668 --> 00:41:01,668
- Uh-oh! Out of control.

1113
00:41:05,276 --> 00:41:07,228
- What's going to become of us now?

1114
00:41:07,228 --> 00:41:08,772
- Oh, everything's about you, isn't it?

1115
00:41:08,772 --> 00:41:11,093
- When log float rides go horribly wrong!

1116
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:13,843
- You may get burnt on this ride.

1117
00:41:15,723 --> 00:41:18,471
- Uh, there's a flaming
moose blocking traffic

1118
00:41:18,471 --> 00:41:20,212
on I-35, W, Northbound.

1119
00:41:20,212 --> 00:41:21,471
- Would somebody please put me out?

1120
00:41:21,471 --> 00:41:23,221
I seem to be on fire!

1121
00:41:24,961 --> 00:41:25,794
- Protect us!

1122
00:41:25,794 --> 00:41:27,300
- Have mercy, dear mistress!

1123
00:41:27,300 --> 00:41:28,550
- Do something!

1124
00:41:29,695 --> 00:41:31,766
- Now, there's something you
don't see every day, Chauncy.

1125
00:41:31,766 --> 00:41:32,599
- Yeah, what's that, Edgar?

1126
00:41:32,599 --> 00:41:34,944
- KISS going bass-fishing.

1127
00:41:34,944 --> 00:41:36,529
- Quite a boat, wouldn't you say?

1128
00:41:36,529 --> 00:41:38,031
- Now that it's finished,
we'll be on our way,

1129
00:41:38,031 --> 00:41:39,657
the minute you give us Annikki.

1130
00:41:39,657 --> 00:41:41,285
- I demand that you make your boat stop!

1131
00:41:41,285 --> 00:41:43,032
- When you release my sister!

1132
00:41:43,032 --> 00:41:44,659
Your only excuse before was because

1133
00:41:44,659 --> 00:41:46,204
your fish wrecked our other boat!

1134
00:41:46,204 --> 00:41:48,287
- Ah, point well taken.

1135
00:41:48,287 --> 00:41:50,929
- You act like I'm the bad guy!

1136
00:41:50,929 --> 00:41:53,449
- I don't know if your
sister is ready for that.

1137
00:41:53,449 --> 00:41:54,791
- She's still upstairs dressing!

1138
00:41:54,791 --> 00:41:56,333
- I warn you, lady of Pohjola!

1139
00:41:56,333 --> 00:41:58,583
You better give us Annikki!

1140
00:41:59,792 --> 00:42:02,718
- Only he has performed
well what I gave him to do,

1141
00:42:02,718 --> 00:42:04,263
and you, what did you do?

1142
00:42:04,263 --> 00:42:05,518
- Yeah!

1143
00:42:05,518 --> 00:42:08,361
- I've heard you make magic too!

1144
00:42:08,361 --> 00:42:09,584
- Hell, I made the horse!

1145
00:42:09,584 --> 00:42:12,713
- What are you talking about, what magic!

1146
00:42:12,713 --> 00:42:14,380
- I mean, the Sampo!

1147
00:42:15,314 --> 00:42:17,102
- [All] Dun dun dun!

1148
00:42:17,102 --> 00:42:18,358
- Have you anything in you heart...

1149
00:42:18,358 --> 00:42:19,941
- Forge a Sampo!

1150
00:42:19,941 --> 00:42:22,504
Or you'll never see the face
of your pretty sister again.

1151
00:42:22,504 --> 00:42:23,965
- Can we see the other parts?

1152
00:42:23,965 --> 00:42:25,556
- Crimeney, better look up Sampo quick,

1153
00:42:25,556 --> 00:42:26,572
I think she's serious.

1154
00:42:26,572 --> 00:42:27,874
- [Ilmarinen] Louhi,
I'll do anything you ask,

1155
00:42:27,874 --> 00:42:29,124
- Only a Sampo!

1156
00:42:33,732 --> 00:42:36,315
(techno music)

1157
00:42:39,669 --> 00:42:41,742
- No, Tom, you're thinking of a sample.

1158
00:42:41,742 --> 00:42:42,881
S-A-M-P-L-E.

1159
00:42:42,881 --> 00:42:44,711
We're talking about a Sampo, with an O.

1160
00:42:44,711 --> 00:42:45,544
- Oh.

1161
00:42:45,544 --> 00:42:47,109
- Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

1162
00:42:47,109 --> 00:42:49,466
So if a Sampo isn't a small
taste of no-fat cheese

1163
00:42:49,466 --> 00:42:52,112
at the grocery store, then
what, I implore you, is it?

1164
00:42:52,112 --> 00:42:53,370
- [Crow] Well I was
thinking that maybe a Sampo

1165
00:42:53,370 --> 00:42:55,041
is a really good can opener.

1166
00:42:55,041 --> 00:42:57,151
- [Tom] No, I think it's
a strapless evening gown!

1167
00:42:57,151 --> 00:42:59,222
- You think everything is
a strapless evening gown!

1168
00:42:59,222 --> 00:43:00,729
- I just think they're neat, is all.

1169
00:43:00,729 --> 00:43:01,911
What do you think, Joel?

1170
00:43:01,911 --> 00:43:03,857
- Uh, I think a Sampo's
like a hand-hammered

1171
00:43:03,857 --> 00:43:05,767
conch belt with turquoise inlays,

1172
00:43:05,767 --> 00:43:08,655
used to accentuate an oversized blouse?

1173
00:43:08,655 --> 00:43:10,651
- I think it's that dent
between the nose and lip.

1174
00:43:10,651 --> 00:43:13,008
- Well, whatever it is,
that witch wants it more

1175
00:43:13,008 --> 00:43:16,099
than anything, so it must be
some sort of wrinkle cream.

1176
00:43:16,099 --> 00:43:17,239
- Oh, no, I got it.

1177
00:43:17,239 --> 00:43:19,233
Sampo: A progressive new corporation

1178
00:43:19,233 --> 00:43:20,733
with an eye towards the future.

1179
00:43:20,733 --> 00:43:23,382
Sampo is a corporation
for people, by people.

1180
00:43:23,382 --> 00:43:25,251
- I think it increases corn yields.

1181
00:43:25,251 --> 00:43:27,813
- I think it's a nasty
little rubber novelty item,

1182
00:43:27,813 --> 00:43:28,911
if you know what I mean.

1183
00:43:28,911 --> 00:43:29,971
- Well, maybe it's not tangible.

1184
00:43:29,971 --> 00:43:32,655
I mean, maybe Sampo is found
in the laughter of children,

1185
00:43:32,655 --> 00:43:34,727
or in the roar of the tide,

1186
00:43:34,727 --> 00:43:37,086
or in the capacity to love and be loved.

1187
00:43:37,086 --> 00:43:37,919
- No, I know.

1188
00:43:37,919 --> 00:43:40,175
I think Sampo is a new
high-energy prop comic.

1189
00:43:40,175 --> 00:43:41,516
You know, like, "Ladies and gentlemen,

1190
00:43:41,516 --> 00:43:44,280
"The Funny Bone is proud to
present funny man Sampo!"

1191
00:43:44,280 --> 00:43:45,909
- Well, one thing's for sure, gentlemen.

1192
00:43:45,909 --> 00:43:48,509
The US of A still makes
the best damn Sampos

1193
00:43:48,509 --> 00:43:51,273
on the market, and I mean
nobody is going to change that!

1194
00:43:51,273 --> 00:43:52,209
- I've got it.

1195
00:43:52,209 --> 00:43:54,484
It's fresh, it's sassy,
it's free, it's me!

1196
00:43:54,484 --> 00:43:56,966
It's an exciting new fragrance
by Prince Machipelli!

1197
00:43:56,966 --> 00:43:58,226
- Oh no.

1198
00:43:58,226 --> 00:43:59,408
- Maybe not.

1199
00:43:59,408 --> 00:44:00,911
- Well, to be honest, everybody,

1200
00:44:00,911 --> 00:44:02,619
we don't know what a Sampo is.

1201
00:44:02,619 --> 00:44:03,452
- Not a clue.

1202
00:44:03,452 --> 00:44:04,733
- If you know what a Sampo is,

1203
00:44:04,733 --> 00:44:06,647
write it down on a piece
of paper, throw it away

1204
00:44:06,647 --> 00:44:07,950
and then try not to think about it.

1205
00:44:07,950 --> 00:44:09,416
You'll be glad you did!

1206
00:44:09,416 --> 00:44:10,303
- [All] Sampo!

1207
00:44:10,303 --> 00:44:11,239
(siren buzzing)

1208
00:44:11,239 --> 00:44:12,072
- Oh, movies!

1209
00:44:12,072 --> 00:44:13,325
- We've got movies, oh, let's go!

1210
00:44:13,325 --> 00:44:14,163
- Sampo!

1211
00:44:14,163 --> 00:44:18,163
(doors whirring, clanking open)

1212
00:44:21,326 --> 00:44:22,743
- Ding! Sampo up!

1213
00:44:24,633 --> 00:44:27,358
- Oh, geez, what a day.

1214
00:44:27,358 --> 00:44:29,145
- You know, I really
admire how you stood firm

1215
00:44:29,145 --> 00:44:30,785
on the Sampo issue, your witchiness.

1216
00:44:30,785 --> 00:44:32,617
You didn't give an inch,
and I really admire that.

1217
00:44:32,617 --> 00:44:34,491
- We'd like to show you how
we maximized the warehouse

1218
00:44:34,491 --> 00:44:36,365
to increase Sampo shipments!

1219
00:44:36,365 --> 00:44:37,624
- Yes, it's really exciting.

1220
00:44:37,624 --> 00:44:39,457
I think you should come
and take a look at it.

1221
00:44:39,457 --> 00:44:40,290
- Well?

1222
00:44:40,290 --> 00:44:41,937
- I must have a wisp of lamb's wool,

1223
00:44:41,937 --> 00:44:43,240
a feather from a swan,

1224
00:44:43,240 --> 00:44:44,546
and a barley corn!

1225
00:44:44,546 --> 00:44:45,807
- You hear this guy?

1226
00:44:45,807 --> 00:44:48,083
- Get him the smallest of the flock,

1227
00:44:48,083 --> 00:44:51,222
and a swan, and whole bushel of barley!

1228
00:44:51,222 --> 00:44:53,139
- And some mini donuts!

1229
00:44:55,344 --> 00:44:58,659
(Tom humming along to music)

1230
00:44:58,659 --> 00:45:00,410
- Um, can we get married?

1231
00:45:00,410 --> 00:45:01,577
We're in love.

1232
00:45:02,449 --> 00:45:03,954
- Nobody asked for a goose,

1233
00:45:03,954 --> 00:45:06,037
you take that right away!

1234
00:45:10,253 --> 00:45:14,420
- Aw, now somebody's sweater
is gonna have a big flaw!

1235
00:45:17,302 --> 00:45:19,741
- You put your feather in before the wool?

1236
00:45:19,741 --> 00:45:20,574
Hmm.

1237
00:45:24,368 --> 00:45:27,235
- With this wool will I clothe you.

1238
00:45:27,235 --> 00:45:30,208
- With these teeth will you bite me.

1239
00:45:30,208 --> 00:45:32,696
- With this barley will I nourish you.

1240
00:45:32,696 --> 00:45:35,873
- Oh, he's making Chex party mix.

1241
00:45:35,873 --> 00:45:39,789
- Ladies and gentlemen, the
magic of Ulysses S. Grant!

1242
00:45:39,789 --> 00:45:40,789
- The Sampo!

1243
00:45:41,745 --> 00:45:42,578
Sampo!

1244
00:45:44,427 --> 00:45:45,974
Sampo!

1245
00:45:45,974 --> 00:45:47,724
- Sampo means flavor!

1246
00:45:49,510 --> 00:45:51,258
- Now give me

1247
00:45:51,258 --> 00:45:54,107
the fire that burned in the clouds!

1248
00:45:54,107 --> 00:45:55,450
- How dare you!

1249
00:45:55,450 --> 00:45:56,550
Don't mention that!

1250
00:45:56,550 --> 00:45:57,733
- It's dirty!

1251
00:45:57,733 --> 00:45:59,157
- You want the Sampo?

1252
00:45:59,157 --> 00:46:01,759
That is the only fire I can forge it in.

1253
00:46:01,759 --> 00:46:03,671
It has to be the heavenly flame.

1254
00:46:03,671 --> 00:46:04,972
- Is it hot in here?

1255
00:46:04,972 --> 00:46:06,802
- I wonder if this is some trick,

1256
00:46:06,802 --> 00:46:09,719
to deprive me of the heavenly fire.

1257
00:46:11,034 --> 00:46:12,337
- But we won't have much use for that

1258
00:46:12,337 --> 00:46:13,437
if he makes the mill!

1259
00:46:13,437 --> 00:46:14,781
Give him the fire!

1260
00:46:14,781 --> 00:46:15,614
- We'll be able to have

1261
00:46:15,614 --> 00:46:17,166
as much flour as we want without grain!

1262
00:46:17,166 --> 00:46:18,472
- And we'll be able to have salt!

1263
00:46:18,472 --> 00:46:21,158
- And we'll be able to
make silver and gold!

1264
00:46:21,158 --> 00:46:23,851
(all clamoring)

1265
00:46:23,851 --> 00:46:25,687
- My spin doctors.

1266
00:46:25,687 --> 00:46:28,331
- Go and fetch the heavenly
flame for him, then.

1267
00:46:28,331 --> 00:46:30,657
- But someone stay here
to answer the phones!

1268
00:46:30,657 --> 00:46:32,737
- Boy, she's really broken
through the glass ceiling, huh?

1269
00:46:32,737 --> 00:46:33,570
- Yeah.

1270
00:46:36,523 --> 00:46:40,273
(Tom singing along to music)

1271
00:46:41,453 --> 00:46:42,923
- Yeah, yesterday's soap.

1272
00:46:42,923 --> 00:46:45,200
We're trying to get rid of it.

1273
00:46:45,200 --> 00:46:46,746
- Oh, it looks like Caligula in here.

1274
00:46:46,746 --> 00:46:48,913
- How would you know that?

1275
00:46:51,060 --> 00:46:52,893
The soup has a escort?

1276
00:46:55,500 --> 00:46:56,500
- Good soup.

1277
00:47:00,212 --> 00:47:02,246
(grunting)

1278
00:47:02,246 --> 00:47:03,832
- Here, ditch this flaming skull for me,

1279
00:47:03,832 --> 00:47:06,761
I don't know how that got in there.

1280
00:47:06,761 --> 00:47:07,942
- Nice weight.

1281
00:47:07,942 --> 00:47:08,775
- Mm-hmm.

1282
00:47:08,775 --> 00:47:09,982
- Real good flame.

1283
00:47:09,982 --> 00:47:10,815
- Mm-hmm.

1284
00:47:14,883 --> 00:47:16,420
- Put all your idle people to work,

1285
00:47:16,420 --> 00:47:17,557
I'll need their help.

1286
00:47:17,557 --> 00:47:20,053
Tell them to work the bellows!

1287
00:47:20,053 --> 00:47:21,643
- You heard what he said!

1288
00:47:21,643 --> 00:47:23,435
- Saul Bellows, get to work!

1289
00:47:23,435 --> 00:47:24,518
- No, no, aw.

1290
00:47:28,559 --> 00:47:30,059
- Is it Sampo yet?

1291
00:47:32,440 --> 00:47:35,940
- Now, be careful, this plate is very hot.

1292
00:47:41,795 --> 00:47:43,795
- So how does this work?

1293
00:47:45,089 --> 00:47:49,321
- Hey, let me know when you need a break.

1294
00:47:49,321 --> 00:47:50,742
- Mark seven!

1295
00:47:50,742 --> 00:47:52,375
Mark seven!

1296
00:47:52,375 --> 00:47:54,330
Oh, mark seven, damnit!

1297
00:47:54,330 --> 00:47:55,754
Mark seven!

1298
00:47:55,754 --> 00:47:58,337
- Riam trolls, working for you!

1299
00:47:59,259 --> 00:48:01,132
- Where's a friggin' Sampo,

1300
00:48:01,132 --> 00:48:03,737
(continues garbling)

1301
00:48:03,737 --> 00:48:06,565
- Uh, Steve, honey, why don't
you go get Daddy a beer.

1302
00:48:06,565 --> 00:48:09,620
- You said you'd make
the mill, where is it?

1303
00:48:09,620 --> 00:48:11,448
- The men can't make the fire hot enough.

1304
00:48:11,448 --> 00:48:14,376
- Sure, blame my department.

1305
00:48:14,376 --> 00:48:16,206
- Keep working, you sluggards!

1306
00:48:16,206 --> 00:48:19,508
Pump the bellows, make the flames leap up!

1307
00:48:19,508 --> 00:48:20,976
- We're doing our best, Mistress.

1308
00:48:20,976 --> 00:48:23,559
- He's got a cocktail dress on!

1309
00:48:30,013 --> 00:48:34,979
- Ah, it's not done, must have
been frozen in the middle.

1310
00:48:34,979 --> 00:48:37,504
- He's got delusions of grandeur.

1311
00:48:37,504 --> 00:48:40,004
- Hey, it's like urban cowboy.

1312
00:48:47,771 --> 00:48:48,604
- Oh, boy.

1313
00:48:48,604 --> 00:48:50,120
How's that beer coming, Stevie?

1314
00:48:50,120 --> 00:48:51,510
- Work harder!

1315
00:48:51,510 --> 00:48:53,603
Get the heat up!

1316
00:48:53,603 --> 00:48:55,067
Faster, faster!

1317
00:48:55,067 --> 00:48:57,389
- Get off, Todd, come on, I'm serious!

1318
00:48:57,389 --> 00:48:58,222
Come on!

1319
00:48:58,222 --> 00:49:00,151
- Oh, they think I'm working,
that's the beauty part!

1320
00:49:00,151 --> 00:49:00,984
- Woohoo!

1321
00:49:04,398 --> 00:49:06,883
Oh, I hate this infernal routine!

1322
00:49:06,883 --> 00:49:08,506
- Burn, baby, burn!

1323
00:49:08,506 --> 00:49:09,673
Disco Inferno!

1324
00:49:14,818 --> 00:49:18,651
- Oh, the guy on top
must be the shop steward.

1325
00:49:19,580 --> 00:49:22,795
- Will someone please get the phone?

1326
00:49:22,795 --> 00:49:26,795
- Kids come running for
the rich taste of Sampo!

1327
00:49:27,770 --> 00:49:29,318
(all scream)

1328
00:49:29,318 --> 00:49:33,485
- Be careful, that's nitric
acid, we don't have very much.

1329
00:49:35,375 --> 00:49:36,263
(all screaming)

1330
00:49:36,263 --> 00:49:38,828
- Oh, I hate this school lunch program.

1331
00:49:38,828 --> 00:49:42,128
- Water's considered a vegetable.

1332
00:49:42,128 --> 00:49:45,394
- This is why I don't make
Sampos except on holidays.

1333
00:49:45,394 --> 00:49:46,742
- Hey, can we help?

1334
00:49:46,742 --> 00:49:50,454
- You can help by setting the table.

1335
00:49:50,454 --> 00:49:52,121
- Sorry, Sampos off.

1336
00:49:53,262 --> 00:49:54,095
- Sampo!

1337
00:49:54,095 --> 00:49:56,522
- Ask for it by name.

1338
00:49:56,522 --> 00:49:57,355
- Sampo!

1339
00:49:57,355 --> 00:49:59,107
- Ask for it by name.

1340
00:49:59,107 --> 00:50:00,856
- Eh, that's a Sampo, huh?

1341
00:50:00,856 --> 00:50:02,075
- Sampo!

1342
00:50:02,075 --> 00:50:03,157
- You know.

1343
00:50:03,157 --> 00:50:05,029
- Ray Nitschke?

1344
00:50:05,029 --> 00:50:06,699
- Do you get wafers with it?

1345
00:50:06,699 --> 00:50:09,341
- You don't get bleeding wafers with it!

1346
00:50:09,341 --> 00:50:11,094
- It's very impressive.

1347
00:50:11,094 --> 00:50:12,735
But how do I know it works?

1348
00:50:12,735 --> 00:50:14,521
- Well, you just plug
it into the wall outlet,

1349
00:50:14,521 --> 00:50:16,269
and turn it on.

1350
00:50:16,269 --> 00:50:18,852
- Let there be gold, and flour,

1351
00:50:20,717 --> 00:50:21,814
and salt!

1352
00:50:21,814 --> 00:50:25,647
- Of course, I recommend
the service contract.

1353
00:50:29,525 --> 00:50:33,786
- Still, I think it would
look better by the couch.

1354
00:50:33,786 --> 00:50:36,634
- Sorry I doubted your Sampo.

1355
00:50:36,634 --> 00:50:39,217
(men cheering)

1356
00:50:41,572 --> 00:50:43,356
- Boy, I thought there'd
be more people around

1357
00:50:43,356 --> 00:50:44,415
the gold part of this thing,

1358
00:50:44,415 --> 00:50:46,364
but the line's really
not that long, you know?

1359
00:50:46,364 --> 00:50:47,464
- This is what it would have been like

1360
00:50:47,464 --> 00:50:49,464
if Perot would have won.

1361
00:50:50,523 --> 00:50:51,940
- Oh, great, rock salt!

1362
00:50:51,940 --> 00:50:55,190
We'll never slip on the driveway again!

1363
00:50:57,569 --> 00:50:59,498
- Makes you think, don't it, honey?

1364
00:50:59,498 --> 00:51:01,044
- Nice to see them so happy.

1365
00:51:01,044 --> 00:51:01,877
- Yup.

1366
00:51:04,178 --> 00:51:06,048
- The manual's in the box, and, uh,

1367
00:51:06,048 --> 00:51:08,400
first upgrade's free.

1368
00:51:08,400 --> 00:51:10,110
- Now give us back Annikki.

1369
00:51:10,110 --> 00:51:11,655
- Oh, she's home already.

1370
00:51:11,655 --> 00:51:15,074
- Alright, I will give your
pretty sister back to you now.

1371
00:51:15,074 --> 00:51:17,991
- I must warn you, she's aged some.

1372
00:51:20,662 --> 00:51:23,329
- Wait, that's the wrong sister.

1373
00:51:24,446 --> 00:51:28,613
- Help yourself a heapin'
helpin' of sweet Annikki.

1374
00:51:32,258 --> 00:51:33,275
- Annikki!

1375
00:51:33,275 --> 00:51:34,740
- Do I know you?

1376
00:51:34,740 --> 00:51:35,922
- Lemminkainen!

1377
00:51:35,922 --> 00:51:39,057
- You're not as cute as I remember!

1378
00:51:39,057 --> 00:51:40,474
On a clear day...

1379
00:51:45,405 --> 00:51:46,832
- Annikki!

1380
00:51:46,832 --> 00:51:48,249
My little sister!

1381
00:51:49,361 --> 00:51:51,397
- Take that creature away from my palace!

1382
00:51:51,397 --> 00:51:52,539
- [Joel] Oh, killjoy.

1383
00:51:52,539 --> 00:51:56,723
- I want her gone with
all those nasty flowers!

1384
00:51:56,723 --> 00:52:00,473
- Don't worry, lady,
we're out of here, gosh!

1385
00:52:03,434 --> 00:52:05,106
- Oh hey, Missus, the
Sampo stopped working,

1386
00:52:05,106 --> 00:52:08,077
and we didn't get the service contract.

1387
00:52:08,077 --> 00:52:10,069
- Smash them, take them away!

1388
00:52:10,069 --> 00:52:11,902
- And I want them all inventoried, too!

1389
00:52:11,902 --> 00:52:14,420
- We don't want them here,
the evil stunning flowers!

1390
00:52:14,420 --> 00:52:17,121
- Man, I wonder what her
Myers-Briggs test was like.

1391
00:52:17,121 --> 00:52:18,664
- How were you ever able to rescue me

1392
00:52:18,664 --> 00:52:19,963
from that wicked creature?

1393
00:52:19,963 --> 00:52:21,957
- Well, I had to make this
boat all by myself, and...

1394
00:52:21,957 --> 00:52:23,260
- Hey, leave my sister alone.

1395
00:52:23,260 --> 00:52:26,817
- Your brother, Ilmarinen, made a Sampo,

1396
00:52:26,817 --> 00:52:28,757
and left it with the wicked witch,

1397
00:52:28,757 --> 00:52:30,143
in place of you.

1398
00:52:30,143 --> 00:52:31,443
- A Sampo?

1399
00:52:31,443 --> 00:52:32,907
- You mean one of those
big things that makes

1400
00:52:32,907 --> 00:52:34,250
gold and salt and stuff?

1401
00:52:34,250 --> 00:52:35,083
- Yeah.

1402
00:52:37,421 --> 00:52:38,926
- You mean the new '92 Sampo

1403
00:52:38,926 --> 00:52:40,435
- with the leather interior?
- [Annikki] And because of me,

1404
00:52:40,435 --> 00:52:44,126
he deprived our people of
their rightful treasure?

1405
00:52:44,126 --> 00:52:46,159
- I am returning to Pohjola,

1406
00:52:46,159 --> 00:52:48,801
and I shall recover the Sampo.

1407
00:52:48,801 --> 00:52:50,230
- No, Ilmarinen!

1408
00:52:50,230 --> 00:52:51,954
I am going back for it, now!

1409
00:52:51,954 --> 00:52:53,867
- No, well, I think a
better plan would be to go

1410
00:52:53,867 --> 00:52:55,693
back and get supplies--hey!

1411
00:52:55,693 --> 00:52:57,240
- Hey, he's got pure wool on,

1412
00:52:57,240 --> 00:52:59,277
he's gonna shrink right up!

1413
00:52:59,277 --> 00:53:01,713
(waves crashing)

1414
00:53:01,713 --> 00:53:03,829
- Try the cleaning power
of new Lemminkainen

1415
00:53:03,829 --> 00:53:05,496
in your rinse cycle!

1416
00:53:10,304 --> 00:53:12,400
- This is it, isn't it?

1417
00:53:12,400 --> 00:53:13,233
- Yeah.

1418
00:53:13,233 --> 00:53:14,066
Think so.

1419
00:53:15,784 --> 00:53:17,450
- Oh, really love the new Sampo!

1420
00:53:17,450 --> 00:53:19,569
No buyer's remorse here, witchy-poo!

1421
00:53:19,569 --> 00:53:21,569
- Who's hungry for salt?

1422
00:53:23,065 --> 00:53:25,465
- Oh, geez, I better plan this, let's see.

1423
00:53:25,465 --> 00:53:27,216
Oh, gotta take the Sampo, it's my dad's.

1424
00:53:27,216 --> 00:53:28,148
No, damn!

1425
00:53:28,148 --> 00:53:29,124
Sampo repair!

1426
00:53:29,124 --> 00:53:30,140
(clears throat)

1427
00:53:30,140 --> 00:53:31,968
Might I just pop in and grab my Sampo?

1428
00:53:31,968 --> 00:53:32,801
No, darn!

1429
00:53:34,902 --> 00:53:36,493
- Oh no, they really like it.

1430
00:53:36,493 --> 00:53:38,360
I was hoping they wouldn't
be getting into the Sampo,

1431
00:53:38,360 --> 00:53:39,443
no such luck.

1432
00:53:40,558 --> 00:53:41,869
- Mmm, a good heft.

1433
00:53:41,869 --> 00:53:43,945
- I caught you, you filthy wretch,

1434
00:53:43,945 --> 00:53:45,249
trying to steal my gold!

1435
00:53:45,249 --> 00:53:46,305
- No, I wasn't!

1436
00:53:46,305 --> 00:53:47,282
- Catch him!

1437
00:53:47,282 --> 00:53:48,848
Don't let him get away!

1438
00:53:48,848 --> 00:53:51,922
Find him and throw him in the machine!

1439
00:53:51,922 --> 00:53:55,605
- Hey Tony, come on,
it's me, your roommate!

1440
00:53:55,605 --> 00:53:56,772
- Monkey pile.

1441
00:53:58,460 --> 00:53:59,293
Phew, ugh!

1442
00:54:00,381 --> 00:54:02,210
That was a mistake.

1443
00:54:02,210 --> 00:54:04,002
- That was the chile relleno wind.

1444
00:54:04,002 --> 00:54:04,835
- Ew!

1445
00:54:06,198 --> 00:54:07,092
- Ouch.

1446
00:54:07,092 --> 00:54:08,799
- Who let the mist out?

1447
00:54:08,799 --> 00:54:11,442
It blinds me, so I cannot see.

1448
00:54:11,442 --> 00:54:14,172
Back into thy bag, mist, I conjure thee,

1449
00:54:14,172 --> 00:54:15,959
back into thy bag.
(Joel coughing)

1450
00:54:15,959 --> 00:54:17,301
- Why did thee even have the mist,

1451
00:54:17,301 --> 00:54:19,619
if it bugs thee so much?

1452
00:54:19,619 --> 00:54:23,786
- It's kinda like a giant
Neo-Synephrine bag, isn't it?

1453
00:54:25,887 --> 00:54:28,205
(witch screams)

1454
00:54:28,205 --> 00:54:29,038
- Ma'am?

1455
00:54:29,913 --> 00:54:33,292
- Where is the many-colored
dome of the Sampo?

1456
00:54:33,292 --> 00:54:36,094
- Ma'am, the dome is an
option that you did not order.

1457
00:54:36,094 --> 00:54:38,089
- After him, and bring him back here!

1458
00:54:38,089 --> 00:54:41,955
- Ah, I can never just sit
back and enjoy my Sampo!

1459
00:54:41,955 --> 00:54:44,538
(men groaning)

1460
00:54:47,869 --> 00:54:50,036
- Hey, it's nice out here!

1461
00:54:53,260 --> 00:54:55,349
- Ah, there he is!

1462
00:54:55,349 --> 00:54:56,690
- Miss America!

1463
00:54:56,690 --> 00:54:58,073
- Destroy Ilamiren!

1464
00:54:58,073 --> 00:54:59,007
Destroy Lemminkainen's boat!

1465
00:54:59,007 --> 00:55:00,061
Release them!

1466
00:55:00,061 --> 00:55:03,599
Let the winds rush over
and destroy this fiend!

1467
00:55:03,599 --> 00:55:05,266
- Fly, monkeys, fly!

1468
00:55:08,864 --> 00:55:11,020
- Oh, now why does this always happen

1469
00:55:11,020 --> 00:55:12,687
at 4:30 on a Friday?

1470
00:55:13,989 --> 00:55:17,156
- Lemminkainen bold, exciting and new!

1471
00:55:19,890 --> 00:55:22,140
- Aguire, the wrath of God!

1472
00:55:25,215 --> 00:55:26,597
- I'm gonna get a bigger boat, right?

1473
00:55:26,597 --> 00:55:30,382
Yeah, we're gonna get a
bigger boat, definitely.

1474
00:55:30,382 --> 00:55:31,562
- Make the witch a Sampo,

1475
00:55:31,562 --> 00:55:34,562
what the heck was I thinking anyway?

1476
00:55:35,750 --> 00:55:38,027
- Wind, with Matthew
Muldeen and Jennifer Grey.

1477
00:55:38,027 --> 00:55:39,277
- Now on video.

1478
00:55:41,973 --> 00:55:43,800
- Hey, it looks just like
the statue of Iwo Jima,

1479
00:55:43,800 --> 00:55:45,063
if you cross your eyes and get the poles

1480
00:55:45,063 --> 00:55:46,980
with all of those guys.

1481
00:55:48,598 --> 00:55:49,452
- Hold on Buck!

1482
00:55:49,452 --> 00:55:51,768
Hold onto the boat, Bucky!

1483
00:55:51,768 --> 00:55:53,638
- Anybody got any Dramamine?

1484
00:55:53,638 --> 00:55:55,224
(gagging)

1485
00:55:55,224 --> 00:55:59,391
- Ladies and gentlemen,
the Swedish Moses of soul.

1486
00:56:03,280 --> 00:56:06,447
- There's got to be a morning after...

1487
00:56:09,648 --> 00:56:11,495
- The boat is wrecked!

1488
00:56:11,495 --> 00:56:13,527
- Don't get short with me, dope!

1489
00:56:13,527 --> 00:56:14,386
- It's wrecked!

1490
00:56:14,386 --> 00:56:15,689
(all clamoring loudly)

1491
00:56:15,689 --> 00:56:17,275
- Yeah right, Madonna and her dancers

1492
00:56:17,275 --> 00:56:19,108
get along really good.

1493
00:56:21,462 --> 00:56:23,703
- You still can't let go
of the Sampo, can you?

1494
00:56:23,703 --> 00:56:25,036
Let it go, Sven.

1495
00:56:27,361 --> 00:56:29,436
- Um, Dad said I could use the car.

1496
00:56:29,436 --> 00:56:30,853
You got the keys?

1497
00:56:31,848 --> 00:56:34,465
- He will be coming home soon,

1498
00:56:34,465 --> 00:56:36,330
and I promise you I will dance with you

1499
00:56:36,330 --> 00:56:37,508
at your wedding feast.

1500
00:56:37,508 --> 00:56:38,341
- Oh.

1501
00:56:38,341 --> 00:56:40,508
Give me the good news now.

1502
00:56:42,305 --> 00:56:43,767
- Our father, who art,

1503
00:56:43,767 --> 00:56:44,661
Huh?

1504
00:56:44,661 --> 00:56:46,407
- Woe! Oh, woe!

1505
00:56:46,407 --> 00:56:51,040
Your brave son Lemminkainen
has met his death.

1506
00:56:51,040 --> 00:56:52,955
- It can't be true!

1507
00:56:52,955 --> 00:56:54,038
My son lives.

1508
00:56:55,149 --> 00:56:57,482
- Coo-coo, coo-coo, coo-coo.

1509
00:56:58,646 --> 00:57:00,717
- Oh, she is off the beam.

1510
00:57:00,717 --> 00:57:02,427
- I see a kidney.

1511
00:57:02,427 --> 00:57:03,427
- I do, yeah.

1512
00:57:06,420 --> 00:57:09,214
- Heathcliff! Catherine!

1513
00:57:09,214 --> 00:57:11,940
- Have pity on a mother's prayer.

1514
00:57:11,940 --> 00:57:14,544
Friend of the four winds of Heaven.

1515
00:57:14,544 --> 00:57:15,851
- Um, have we met?

1516
00:57:15,851 --> 00:57:19,047
- Can you tell me what's
become of my brave son?

1517
00:57:19,047 --> 00:57:21,684
- I have troubles enough of my own.

1518
00:57:21,684 --> 00:57:24,284
The men strip my bark for making baskets.

1519
00:57:24,284 --> 00:57:26,441
The children break my branches for brooms.

1520
00:57:26,441 --> 00:57:28,507
How should I know anything about your son?

1521
00:57:28,507 --> 00:57:29,848
- Geez, sorry I asked!

1522
00:57:29,848 --> 00:57:31,681
- Birch, birch, birch.

1523
00:57:33,549 --> 00:57:35,057
- Now get out of my office!

1524
00:57:35,057 --> 00:57:39,777
Miss Jenkins, I pay you
to screen these people!

1525
00:57:39,777 --> 00:57:42,583
- I see a past president
who shall remain nameless.

1526
00:57:42,583 --> 00:57:43,597
- Oh you mean,

1527
00:57:43,597 --> 00:57:44,827
- Chester Arthur.

1528
00:57:44,827 --> 00:57:46,250
- Hey, uh, lady!

1529
00:57:46,250 --> 00:57:49,425
I'm a nice big pine that
you could pray to, maybe.

1530
00:57:49,425 --> 00:57:50,258
Maybe?

1531
00:57:51,501 --> 00:57:53,901
- Tell me, old wandering road,

1532
00:57:53,901 --> 00:57:56,901
have pity on a poor mother's sorrow!

1533
00:57:58,207 --> 00:58:01,465
Do you know what happened to my son?

1534
00:58:01,465 --> 00:58:05,290
- Um, b-oh I'll put the
word out on the street!

1535
00:58:05,290 --> 00:58:06,957
Oh, I am the street.

1536
00:58:09,322 --> 00:58:11,678
- Excuse me, I'm kind of stuck in a rut.

1537
00:58:11,678 --> 00:58:15,661
- Mother Teresa, in a role
that will inspire you!

1538
00:58:15,661 --> 00:58:18,550
- You should have pity on me!

1539
00:58:18,550 --> 00:58:20,459
I am the road!

1540
00:58:20,459 --> 00:58:24,568
- I didn't appreciate what
Kerouac said about me!

1541
00:58:24,568 --> 00:58:27,014
- ...to find your wandering son.

1542
00:58:27,014 --> 00:58:27,910
